   151	*Fiske. Force Path. I've charted Force on five floors and none of them used it like this. Everybody else builds force and delivers it: gather, commit, strike. Fiske doesn't strike with it. She puts it somewhere. Three uses of the Path in eleven minutes, the fewest I've charted on these rings, and every one of them went into the floor in front of his next step instead of into him. She's not stronger than the people she beats. She's earlier. She sees where they're going and closes the door before they get there.*
   152	
   153	*Price: she has to see first. For the first minute and a half she's collecting, and she opens badly, twice today, because she hadn't finished reading him. Somebody she's never seen could take her early.*
   154	
   155	*After that, in this bracket, I don't think anybody can. The bracket knows it too, and comes out against her already beaten.*
   156	
   157	*Two years, and the whole Copper column has had its turn at her. She's fought every answer it has. There aren't any left.*
