editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/BOOK_MAP.md:197:Track injuries forward: Cael's shoulder after the baseline (3 days) and again after the evaluation; the hip after the evaluation (3 days minimum); the Compression bone hum after the pin (day 4). Lira's hip from the semifinal (nine days into the final) and after the final (4 days off). Brom's knee from the final and the strapped knuckles. Rule from the seat: a learning fight leaves a correction that can be attempted again, and a loss buys knowledge, not a disguised victory.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/BOOK_MAP.md:203:Sentence mean 14.6 (median 11; wide spread, σ ≈26); **≈28% of sentences ≤5 words**; ≈3.3% ≥40 words. Paragraph median ≈18 words (mean ≈27). Scene breaks about every 950 words (≈5 per chapter). Flesch Reading Ease ≈72, FK grade ≈6.8. Current-edition baseline is sentence mean 17.5, paragraph median 44, FRE 67, grade 8.3. **The largest single change is paragraphs:** break early and often; keep the log entries as short paragraphs. Section 8 signals stay secondary ("that" below 92 per 10k; adverbs and dialogue tags moderate; combat vocabulary in the background throughout, ≈22 per 10k). Measure after each movement with `python3 editions/monroe-1.3/tools/formula_metrics.py`. Paragraph and scene figures are ASR-inferred proxies; development counts are heuristics.
