editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-002/pre-repair/chapter-13.md:161:Four short sentences, against six days without proper sleep and an hour of held breath and a shoulder that would complain until the week was out. He waited to be let down by them, and was not. There was nothing wrong in any of them. *Consistent across trials* was the only good word the instrument knew how to say, and it had said it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-002/pre-repair/chapter-13.md:213:*He doesn't want to know what I am,* he wrote that night, under the plate. *He wants me to be the same twice running. That's harder than being anything. It's also the first thing anybody's asked of me in a long while that I can actually give.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-13.md:61:And a fortnight ago, in a room with a key outside its door, it had told him a lie by saying nothing.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-13.md:161:Four short sentences, against four bad nights and an hour of held breath and a shoulder that would complain until the week was out. He waited to be let down by them, and was not. There was nothing wrong in any of them. *Consistent across trials* was the only good word the instrument knew how to say, and it had said it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-13.md:213:*He doesn't want to know what I am,* he wrote that night, under the plate. *He wants me to be the same twice running. That's harder than being anything. It's also the first thing anybody's asked of me in a long while that I can actually give.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-002/pre-repair/chapter-12.md:7:He leaned over her shoulder. It was Halcenvane's own copy of the founding clause, with the charter article that carried it set out beneath, and below that the assessment office's standing rule for applying it, in a dry modern hand. He had read all three before. He had read them on the first night, and again in Bracken's room, and again on the night the notice came. He had not read them the way Karis read things, which was as if each word had been put there by somebody who might be lying.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-002/pre-repair/chapter-12.md:17:He walked back to the second quadrangle in the dusk with that sentence going round in his head like a cart wheel, and that night he did not sleep, and the night after he slept very little.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-002/pre-repair/chapter-12.md:27:On the third night he lay looking at the ceiling and worked out, for the first time with complete clarity, the two ways it could be made to cheat.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-002/pre-repair/chapter-12.md:91:In the binder that night he filed it under method. Lira, he thought, would accept that.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-002/pre-repair/chapter-12.md:101:He slept, after that, for the first time in four nights, and woke at the fifth bell with his mind quite clear and one thing still sitting in it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-002/pre-repair/chapter-12.md:131:The night before, Lira took him out to the cracked yard behind the second quadrangle, where nobody went after dark, and made him walk the framework through once at a stroll, with no bursts in it at all.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-002/pre-repair/chapter-12.md:155:"And sleep," said Lira, getting up. "That's an order, not advice. If you turn up in that room having lain awake all night, I'll know, and Gault will know, and the clerk will write it down."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-002/pre-repair/chapter-12.md:213:Of all the things Cael had readied himself for, he had not thought of this one: that the man holding the measure would name, in his first minute and as a matter of routine, the very thing about the measure that had kept Cael awake for three nights.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-12.md:7:He leaned over her shoulder. It was Halcenvane's own copy of the founding clause, with the charter article that carried it set out beneath, and below that the assessment office's standing rule for applying it, in a dry modern hand. He had read all three before, on the first night, and again in Bracken's room, and again on the night the notice came. He had not read them the way Karis read things, which was as if each word had been put there by somebody who might be lying.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-12.md:17:He walked back to the second quadrangle in the dusk with that sentence turning in his head, and for three nights afterward he slept badly.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-12.md:21:By the third night he could see the two ways to cheat it, one low and one high, and he could see neither was right, and he could not yet see what was.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-12.md:23:He put it to the others on the fourth evening, in the common room, because three nights alone with it had taught him he was carrying it badly.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-12.md:77:That night it went into the binder under *method*. Lira, he thought, would accept that.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-12.md:87:He slept, after that, for the first time in four nights, and woke at the fifth bell with his mind quite clear and one thing still sitting in it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-12.md:117:The night before, Lira took him out to the cracked yard behind the second quadrangle, where nobody went after dark, and made him walk the framework through once at a stroll, with no bursts in it at all.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-12.md:141:"And sleep," said Lira, getting up. "That's an order, not advice. If you turn up in that room having lain awake all night, I'll know, and Gault will know, and the clerk will write it down."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-12.md:199:Of all the things Cael had readied himself for, he had not thought of this one: that the man holding the measure would name, in his first minute and as a matter of routine, the very thing about the measure that had kept Cael awake for three nights.

